# tally 2.1.8 P32 (stands), L §8.2 (the round's check, T's g1f_f2_edge_held): a held line prints once per row; a hole
# row carried past the cut prints in its own form (7167d6b4), but a row whose value is computed (cq = bm.cr, a
# scenario's expression row) and comes out a hole prints ?: held: cq = ? (sx_v). 40bd8257 printed the hole there.
=== m.tally
model bm
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
input d: date
input cr: calendar
input cq: calendar
input huge: int

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d = 2026-06-01 "a day"
  huge = 100000000000000000000 "10^20"

version v26
  cite plan
  governs 2026
  known 2026-01-01
  cr = calendar(weekends [sat, sun]) "s"
  cq = calendar(weekends [sat, sun]) "s"

ask f: add_business(d, huge, cq) in sx
=== b2_min_sc.tally
scenario sx over bm
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

version sx_v
  cite plan
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  replace cq = bm.cr "s"
=== expect
f: refused: RUN-LIMIT a day passes 9999-12-31
  world: sx
  held: cq = ? (sx_v), read for 2027-01-01
  cut 2026-12-31
